      "score": 66,
      "comments": 13,
      "author": "olex",
      "published": "2026-08-21T07:47:50Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Standard library 'batteries-included' architectures face maintenance debt, prompting shifts toward modular, independently versioned core ecosystems.",
        "Over-reliance on third-party package registries increases supply-chain vulnerabilities compared to vetted, first-party standard utilities.",
        "Modern runtime design balances minimal core language distributions with officially maintained utility modules to sustain velocity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
